{title: Amazing Grace}
{subtitle: John Newton}
{ccli: 22025}

{start_of_verse}
Amazing [D]grace how [G]sweet the [D]sound
That saved a wretch like [A]me
I [D]once was lost but [G]now am [D]found
Was [D]blind but [A]now I [D]see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
'Twas [D]grace that taught my [G]heart to [D]fear
And grace my fears re-[A]lieved
How [D]precious did that [G]grace ap-[D]pear
The [D]hour I [A]first be-[D]lieved
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Amazing [D]grace how [G]sweet the [D]sound
That [D]saved a [A]wretch like [D]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Through [D]many dangers, [G]toils and [D]snares
I have already [A]come
'Tis [D]grace that brought me [G]safe thus [D]far
And [D]grace will [A]lead me [D]home
{end_of_verse}
